      en: "Pico de São João is a prominent mountain overlooking the bay of São João in the Cantagalo district on the east coast of São Tomé. Its proximity to the sea and its steep slopes give it a dramatic appearance. The mountain is an eroded volcanic cone, its flanks now partly covered with agricultural crops, especially cocoa, and partly with secondary forest. It is closely linked to the history of the nearby Roça São João, a famous plantation that is now a center for culture and gastronomy. The mountain protects the valleys and the bay from the prevailing winds and creates a favorable microclimate. Hikes on Pico de São João are popular as they offer spectacular views of the coast and insights into the intertwined history of plantation economy and nature."
